    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "VictoriaMetrics"
      },
      "description": "How long a write waits for its commitlog entry to become durable \u2014 the fsync cost. This is a DISK SPEED problem when it rises: the device cannot complete the sync fast enough. Compare it against the segment-allocation panel beside it; the two are different failures and the fix for each is different. A FLAT ZERO HERE IS NORMAL and does not mean the panel is broken: under commitlog_sync: periodic, the Cassandra default, the writer never blocks on the fsync, so nothing is recorded. The gauge only carries a value under commitlog_sync: batch or group, where it is the device latency every write pays for. Read one series per node \u2014 this gauge is pre-aggregated on the node and is never summed or averaged across nodes.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
