      "description": "How long a write blocks waiting for a commitlog segment to be handed to it. This is a CAPACITY problem, not a disk-speed one: the commitlog is out of space, so the writer is stalled until an old segment is recycled, and a segment can only be recycled once every memtable holding data in it has been flushed. If this panel is high while Waiting on Commit is flat, do not go looking at the disk \u2014 raise commitlog_total_space, or find the table whose memtable is not flushing (see the memtable row below). Pre-aggregated per node; one series per node, never aggregated.",
