      "description": "On-heap memtable bytes summed across every table matching $keyspace and $table, one series per node. This is the number to compare against memtable_heap_space: when it approaches that limit Cassandra flushes the largest memtable regardless of how full it is. Summing here is legitimate because these are byte gauges, not percentiles \u2014 bytes add, latencies do not. Use it to spot a single node carrying more buffered data than its peers, which usually points at an uneven token range or a hot partition.",
